-- title:
--   ℤ-sections of G have finite index in J₀(p)(ℚ)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime. Write $J_0(p)(\overline{\mathbf Q})$ for `JZero p`, the group of degree-zero divisor classes of the modular function field `modularFunctionFieldBar p` over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, with its Galois action. Let $g \colon G \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ be a morphism of schemes and let $\mathrm{pts}$ be a bijection from $J_0(p)(\overline{\mathbf Q})$ onto the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbf Q} \to G$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ (pairs $(\varphi, \varphi \circ g =$ the structure map$)$), compatible with the Galois action in the sense that $\mathrm{pts}(\sigma \cdot x)$ is $\operatorname{Spec}(\sigma)$ followed by $\mathrm{pts}(x)$ for every $\sigma \in \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbf Q}/\mathbf Q)$ and every $x$. Assume $g$ is separated and locally of finite type, and that the base change of $g$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z[1/p] \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ (the second projection of the pullback of $g$ against $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbf Z \to \mathrm{Localization.Away}\,p$) is proper. Let $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbf Q}$ be a valuation subring with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, let $\Phi$ be a finite abelian group, and let $\mathrm{comp}$ be an additive map from `inertiaInvariants A p`, the subgroup of $J_0(p)(\overline{\mathbf Q})$ fixed by the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbf Q$, to $\Phi$. Assume that every $x$ in these inertia invariants which is fixed by all of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbf Q}/\mathbf Q)$ and satisfies $\mathrm{comp}(x) = 0$ admits an $A$-point $s$ of $G$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ with $\mathrm{pts}(x)$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbf Q})$ followed by $s$. Then the additive subgroup of $J_0(p)(\overline{\mathbf Q})$ generated by the classes $\mathrm{pts}^{-1}$ of the $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-points obtained by base change from sections of $g$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ meets the subgroup of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbf Q}/\mathbf Q)$-fixed points in a subgroup of finite index in that fixed-point subgroup.
--
--   This is the finite-index property required of the Néron identity component data for $J_0(p)$ over $\mathbf Z$: the group generated by the integral sections of $G$ cuts out a finite-index subgroup of $J_0(p)(\mathbf Q)$, the Galois-fixed part of $J_0(p)(\overline{\mathbf Q})$. It is used in assembling the good Néron identity component package for $J_0(p)$, in [`ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronIdentityComponentGood_of_dRModelPackage_of_ffPin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronIdentityComponentGood_of_dRModelPackage_of_ffPin).
